From 631d53db1633d34224c9a82ad9e1364b10c1957b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:48:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] feat(registry): add update_spec for desired-state
 updates

put(expected_version=...) rewrites the whole stored object: a caller
that only wants to change the desired state has to send back status,
conditions, finalizers and observedGeneration it read earlier, and it
cannot tell a spec change (which must bump generation) from a label
change (which must not). The API needs a narrower, race-free entry
point for PUT and PATCH.

update_spec replaces spec, labels and annotations of a resource whose
kind has a registered model, validates the result against that model
and keeps everything the controller owns untouched. The spec is
compared after normalisation, so only a real spec change increments
generation; labels and annotations changes only bump the resource
version, and an update that changes nothing is not written at all.
Checks and write run in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction. Terminating
resources are rejected first (retrying cannot help), then optional uid
and resource version preconditions; the uid catches a resource that
was deleted and re-created under the same name, whose version counts
up from 0 again. Each ConflictError carries a ConflictReason in
details["reason"] so the API can report why it refused the write.
